    guide: [{ heading: "How compound growth is calculated", body: "Compounding accelerates wealth because each interval's proceeds become next interval's foundation according to A = P multiplied by (1+r/f) raised to f times t. Principal P anchors calculation, nominal rate r fuels velocity, frequency f dictates reinvestment rhythm, and tenure t magnifies exponentiation. Benchmark Rs 50,000 at 8% across ten years: yearly rests mature near Rs 1,07,946, quarterly near Rs 1,10,401, monthly near Rs 1,10,982 with Rs 60,982 interest. Frequency matrix illustrates divergence: annual 1 | half-yearly 2 | quarterly 4 | monthly 12. Monthly outpaces yearly by Rs 3,036 despite identical headline rate, demonstrating rest potency. Early years crawl while later years surge as base swells; inspect annual schedule to witness inflection beyond year six. All projections execute privately inside browser storage, assuming immutable rates and uninterrupted tenure. See /terms." }, { heading: "Inputs, frequency and limitations", body: "Supply lump principal, nominal percentage, rest cadence, and duration; calculator returns maturity, aggregate interest, effective yield, and tabular progression without demanding personal identifiers. Model Rs 10,000 at 8% monthly for ten years maturing near Rs 22,196 versus Rs 21,589 yearly, a Rs 607 frequency premium. Contrast lump Rs 50,000 compounding quietly against SIP Rs 5,000 monthly at 12% accumulating near Rs 11.5 lakh from Rs 6 lakh contributions, highlighting installment discipline versus windfall deployment. Idealize constant rates, zero levies, absent inflation, and punctual reinvestment; actual debentures reset coupons, mutual funds fluctuate net values, and taxation erodes harvests. Premature redemption forfeits exponentiation dramatically, especially during terminal years. Validate bank sanction letters for rest definitions, payout versus cumulative options, and penalty clauses. Pair nominal outcomes with /inflation-calculator for purchasing parity and /sip-calculator for installment alternatives. See /terms." }, { heading: "Next steps and common questions", body: "Extend tenure from ten toward fifteen years and Rs 50,000 at 8% monthly leaps from Rs 1,10,982 toward Rs 1,65,346, proving duration outweighs incremental rate hikes. Alternatively elevate rate from 7% to 8% on identical principal and horizon, lifting maturity from Rs 1,02,303 toward Rs 1,10,982. Exploit yearly ledger to identify crossover when interest eclipses principal, then align redemptions with tuition, housing, or retirement milestones. Beware variable coupons, compounding holidays, rounding conventions, and TDS thresholds that truncate advertised yields. Cross-check ambitious projections against conservative 6% scenarios before committing life savings. Document assumptions, export schedules for advisers, and revisit annually as policies evolve. Deepen methodology via /methodology, juxtapose installment strategies at /sip-calculator, and internalize disclaimers at /terms before acting. This exposition educates rather than recommends securities." }]
