    guide: [{ heading: "What simple interest means", body: "Simple interest levies a fixed charge solely on original principal, never on accumulated interest. A $10,000 loan at 5% for 3 years accrues $1,500 interest for $11,500 total and $319 monthly, while 8% jumps to $2,400 interest and $12,400 total. Tenure burden table steadies expectations: | Principal $10k | Rate | Years | Interest | 5% | 3 | $1,500 | 5% | 5 | $2,500 | 8% | 3 | $2,400 |. Short personal advances, dealer flat deals, and bridge facilities quote this transparent style. Our simple interest calculator translates principal, rate, and duration into interest, total, and monthly privately offline. Edge case: partial prepayments mid-tenure require recalculating on reduced principal manually. Limitation: disregards processing levies, late penalties, and reducing-balance conventions. Contrast compounding via /compound-interest-calculator. Foundational maths only, not lending advice. See /terms." }, { heading: "How simple interest is calculated", body: "Simple interest equals principal times rate times time divided by 100, total equals principal plus interest, monthly equals total divided by months. For example, $10,000 times 5 times 3 divided by 100 gives $1,500 interest, $11,500 total, $11,500 over 36 equals $319 monthly. A second illustration: $18,000 at 7% for 5 years gives $6,300 interest, $24,300 total, $405 monthly flat. Flat versus reducing table exposes divergence: | Loan $18k 5yr | Flat total interest | Reducing EMI interest | 7% flat | $6,300 | $6,300 | 7% reducing | $3,380 | $3,380 |. Identical headline rates diverge wildly by method. Edge case: leap-year day counts marginally shift per-diem accruals. Limitation: single fixed rate ignores floating resets, penalty compounding, and fee amortization. Verify amortized reality via /auto-loan-calculator. Instructional estimates only, never credit counsel. See /terms." }, { heading: "Simple interest worked example: $10,000 at 5 percent for 3 years", body: "Enter $10,000 at 5% for 3 years to see $1,500 interest, $11,500 total, and $319 monthly, then try 8% to watch interest leap to $2,400 and monthly to $344. Sensitivity grid aids negotiation: | Rate 3yr $10k | Interest | Monthly | 5% | $1,500 | $319 | 6.5% | $1,950 | $332 | 8% | $2,400 | $344 |. Each point adds roughly $300 interest. Edge case: early settlement in month 20 still owes pro-rata interest to date, not full-term charge, depending on lender rebate policy. Limitation: flat maths excludes origination levies, insurance bundling, GST on fees, and compounding penalties. Explore true amortized cost beside /emi-calculator. Informational planning support only, not professional borrowing guidance before signing loan documents attentively. See /terms." }]
