    guide: [{ heading: "What mortgage overpayment does", body: "Overpayment injects additional principal beyond scheduled EMI, shrinking the interest-bearing balance so subsequent charges fall and tenure compresses. A $250,000 loan at 6% for 30 years normally costs $1,499 EMI and $289,000 interest; adding $200 monthly trims payoff to about 23 years and saves near $70,000. Impact table motivates persistence: | Extra monthly | Payoff | Interest saved | $0 | 30yr | $0 | $200 | 23yr | $70,000 | $400 | 19yr | $110,000 |. Doubling extra nearly doubles redemption. Our mortgage overpayment calculator reveals new payoff date, interest rescued, and months eliminated privately offline. Edge case: lenders capping annual overpayments at 10% force splitting windfalls across January. Limitation: fixed-rate projection ignores resets, penalties, and foregone investment compounding. Contrast refinancing via /refinance-calculator. Prepayment illustration only, not lending advice. See /terms." }, { heading: "How monthly extra versus lump sum is compared", body: "Recurring extras compound every instalment, while isolated lumps slash balance once, so habitual overpayments generally dominate equal totals paid early. For example, $200 monthly ($2,400 yearly) from start on $250,000 at 6% outperforms a solitary $10,000 injection in year 5 by roughly $18,000 saved interest. Strategy face-off table: | Strategy $250k 6% | Total extra 5yr | Interest saved | $200 monthly | $12,000 | $28,000 | $10k lump yr5 | $10,000 | $10,500 | $400 monthly | $24,000 | $52,000 |. Steady discipline beats windfall timing. Edge case: offset-linked mortgages parking cash preserve liquidity while mimicking overpayment mathematically. Limitation: assumes allowance headroom, ignoring early-repayment charges and offset fees. Examine base instalments via /mortgage-calculator. Comparative mechanics only, never personal debt counsel. See /terms." }, { heading: "Overpayment worked example: $250k with $200 extra", body: "Enter $250,000 balance, 6%, 30 years, $200 extra, $5,000 lump to see about $75,000 combined saving, 84 months cut, and payoff in year 23, then raise to $400 extra to approach 19 years and $110,000 saved. Payoff matrix sharpens resolve: | Extra | Lump $5k | Payoff | Saved | $200 | Yes | 23yr | $75,000 | $200 | No | 23.5yr | $70,000 | $400 | No | 19yr | $110,000 |. Lump adds $5,000 incremental rescue. Edge case: directing $200 to 19% cards instead rescues triple interest, so clear revolving first. Limitation: fixed schedule excludes penalties, payment holidays, and tax-relief erosion on deductible interest. Model affordability headroom via /home-affordability-calculator. Informational prepayment walkthrough only, not professional mortgage guidance before overpaying judiciously. See /terms." }]
