    guide: [{ heading: "What a US paycheck estimate shows", body: "A US paycheck projection converts salary or hourly wages into per-period take-home after federal income levy, FICA payroll imposts, state withholding, and 401k deferrals. An $85,000 single salary biweekly nets near $2,380 per check after $9,800 federal, $6,502 FICA, $4,250 state, and $4,000 401k, while $40 hourly at 40 hours ($83,200) nets near $2,330. Frequency table aids cashflow: | Cycle | Checks | $85k net example | Biweekly | 26 | $2,380 | Semimonthly | 24 | $2,575 | Monthly | 12 | $5,150 |. Monthly smooths bills; biweekly accelerates debt snowballs. Our US paycheck calculator spans weekly through monthly cadences privately offline. Edge case: three-paycheck months twice yearly inflate biweekly budgets 50%. Limitation: simplified 5% state proxy ignores graduated California versus zero Texas regimes. Refine annual view via /salary-calculator. Payroll illustration only, not tax advice. See /terms." }, { heading: "How federal, FICA, and state splits are calculated", body: "Federal applies 2026 brackets to salary minus $14,600 single standard deduction, FICA levies 6.2% Social Security to $184,500 wage base plus 1.45% Medicare uncapped, state multiplies simplified percentage. For example, $85,000 minus $14,600 leaves $70,400 federal taxable near $9,800; FICA hits $6,502; 5% state takes $4,250; $4,000 401k further trims federal. Split table: | Levy $85k single | Base | Amount | Federal | $70,400 | $9,800 | FICA | $85,000 | $6,502 | State 5% | $85,000 | $4,250 |. Gross minus trio minus 401k equals net; divide by 26 for biweekly. Edge case: earnings above $184,500 pause Social Security but not Medicare plus 0.9% surcharge past $200,000. Limitation: omits local imposts, credits, catch-up contributions, and W-4 step adjustments. Cross-check annual levy via /income-tax-calculator. Tax mechanics only, never filing counsel. See /terms." }, { heading: "Paycheck worked example: $85k single biweekly net", body: "Enter $85,000 salary, single, biweekly, 5% state, $4,000 401k to see about $2,380 net per check with federal/FICA/state itemization, then lift to $90,000 to watch net climb only $145 despite $192 gross per-check rise due to bracket creep. Comparison grid guides negotiation: | Salary single 5% | Net biweekly | Net monthly | $80,000 | $2,245 | $4,865 | $85,000 | $2,380 | $5,150 | $90,000 | $2,525 | $5,470 |. Five thousand raise nets $3,510 yearly after trio. Edge case: $40 hourly overtime at time-half ($60) for 5 hours adds $300 gross but $195 net after 22% plus FICA. Limitation: excludes municipal levies, dependent credits, pre-tax transit, and bonus supplemental withholding. Plan debt payoff via /debt-payoff-calculator. Informational paycheck walkthrough only, not professional tax guidance before budgeting earnings attentively. See /terms." }]
