    category: "finance",
    faq: [{ question: "Should I choose the new or old tax regime?", answer: "FY 2026-27 keeps the new regime as default with Rs 75,000 standard deduction and no HRA or 80C. The old regime allows HRA and 80C but needs more proof. Pick new for simple pay. Pick old if claims are large. Compare both and see /terms." }, { question: "Why is tax zero up to Rs 12.75 lakh salary?", answer: "Staff pay zero tax to Rs 12,75,000 in FY 2026-27. You subtract Rs 75,000 deduction to reach Rs 12,00,000 taxable. The 87A rebate wipes tax up to Rs 60,000. Above this mark, slabs plus 4% cess apply. This is info only. Consult a CA. See /terms." }, { question: "Does my CTC data stay on this device?", answer: "Yes. CTC TDS math stays on your phone only. Basic PF sums run here offline with no net call and no login. For instance, Rs 10,80,000 stays in-tab, works net-off, and clears on close. Estimates only, not tax advice. See /terms." }, { question: "Why does Rs 13,50,000 CTC suddenly trigger Rs 42,000 tax?", answer: "Because crossing Rs 12,75,000 forfeits 87A shelter, so Rs 13,50,000 minus Rs 75,000 leaves Rs 12,75,000 taxable facing slabs near Rs 60,000 plus 4% cess Rs 2,400, totalling Rs 62,400 versus zero below. Marginal spike exceeds increment. Model Rs 12,75,000 versus Rs 13,50,000 here. See /terms." }, { question: "How do EPF, ESI and gratuity compress monthly in-hand?", answer: "Statutory carve-outs bite before payout, Rs 12,00,000 CTC with Rs 6,00,000 Basic incurs Rs 72,000 EPF (12%), Rs 2,400 professional tax, plus 4.81% gratuity accrual Rs 28,860, leaving Rs 10,96,740 divisible cash before TDS. Sub-Rs 21,000 earners add 0.75% ESI. Reconcile offer letters via /payslip-generator. Payroll maths only, not labour counsel. See /terms." }],
