    guide: [{ heading: "Old vs new regime in FY 2026-27", body: "FY 2026-27 defaults salaried taxpayers to the new 115BAC regime with Rs 75,000 standard deduction, concessional slabs, and Rs 60,000 87A rebate sheltering Rs 12,75,000 gross. It bars HRA exemption, 80C investments, 80D beyond defaults, and home-loan interest set-off. The legacy old regime preserves HRA metro 50% plus 80C Rs 1,50,000, 80D, and steeper slabs demanding documentation. Regime contrast table: | Feature | New default | Old optional | Standard deduction | Rs 75k | Rs 50k | HRA | Nil | Exempt | 80C | Nil | Rs 1.5L |. Clean single-income earners favour new; HRA-heavy Mumbai renters with Rs 3,00,000 claims favour old. Our in-hand salary calculator computes monthly TDS under new rules privately offline. Edge case: senior citizens with medical premiums may still tilt old. Limitation: excludes perquisite valuation, leave encashment slabs, and surcharge tapers. Weigh CTC structuring via /salary-calculator. Regime explainer only, not tax advice. See /terms." }, { heading: "HRA, 80C, and TDS basics", body: "House Rent Allowance, 80C basket, and Tax Deducted at Source interplay defines monthly cash timing. Under old rules, Rs 4,80,000 yearly rent in Mumbai with Rs 6,00,000 Basic yields HRA exemption near Rs 3,00,000 after 10% salary least-of formula; 80C absorbs EPF Rs 72,000 plus PPF top-up to Rs 1,50,000. TDS slices estimated annual liability across 12 payrolls after 87A and cess. Deduction stack table: | Head FY26 new | Benefit | Head old | Benefit | Standard | Rs 75k | Standard | Rs 50k | 87A | Rs 60k to 12.75L | 87A | Lower threshold | EPF | Statutory | 80C | Rs 1.5L |. New regime skips proofs, accelerating payroll. Edge case: job switch merging two Form 16s without declaration duplicates rebate, triggering demand notices. Limitation: flat TDS view ignores advance-tax interest 234B/C and Form 12BB misdeclarations. Generate slips via /payslip-generator. Payroll primer only, not filing counsel. See /terms." }, { heading: "Rs 12.75L zero-tax example", body: "Consider Rs 12,75,000 CTC in FY 2026-27 under new regime: subtract Rs 75,000 standard deduction for Rs 12,00,000 taxable, compute slabs near Rs 60,000, then apply 87A rebate wiping liability to zero plus zero cess. Net monthly in-hand after Rs 72,000 EPF and Rs 2,400 professional tax nears Rs 99,000 before allowances. Cliff table warns progression: | Gross FY26 new | Taxable | Tax plus cess | Rs 12,75,000 | Rs 12,00,000 | Rs 0 | Rs 13,50,000 | Rs 12,75,000 | Rs 62,400 | Rs 15,00,000 | Rs 14,25,000 | Rs 1,05,000 |. Seventy-five thousand extra gross triggers Rs 62,400 levy. Edge case: Rs 21,000 threshold entrants toggle ESI 0.75% employee bite, trimming in-hand Rs 150 monthly. Limitation: simplified TDS ignores gratuity accrual, employer PF matching exclusions, and variable bonus quarterly withholding. Model US parallels via /us-paycheck-calculator. Illustrative computation only, not chartered-accountancy guidance before filing returns carefully. See /terms." }]
